#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""llmt — set up and manage the llm-translators (one venv, one MCP server per translator).

    llmt setup                      guided setup: what to install here, venv, backends, MCP servers
    llmt list                       the translators, what they need, what is installed here
    llmt install KEY... [options]   install translators into the shared venv (and what they use)
    llmt remove KEY...              uninstall translators from the venv
    llmt status [-v] [--json]       versions, submodule commits, backends found
    llmt update [--latest]          pull, check out the pinned (or latest) commits, reinstall; fill config/env
                                    settings not set yet from llmt tune (--no-tune: leave it)
    llmt pin [KEY...] [--commit [--push]]   move the pins to each translator's latest pushed commit
    llmt test [KEY...]              each translator's pytest suite
    llmt bench KEY [NAMES...]       a translator's benchmarks
    llmt alias [--name N] [--rc F]  shell alias that activates the venv (default llmt-venv; old ones commented out)
    llmt tune [KEY...] [--print | --apply]   SLURM use, MPI ranks and timeouts for this machine, from its cores
    llmt jobs [KEY...]              the translators' SLURM jobs on this machine (queued, running)
    llmt env [--edit] [--system]    the settings file (config/env; yours in a shared release; --system: the machine's)

Shared install for all users (docs/SHARED.md), admin commands run from a checkout:
    llmt deploy [KEY...] [--test] [--bench] [--prefix P]   build a release in /opt/llm-translators and switch to it
    llmt releases | rollback [RELEASE] | gc [--keep N]     list, switch back, remove unused old releases
    llmt mcp setup                  choose local / remote (ssh) / auto (router) / existing install / none per translator
    llmt router setup | status [KEY...]   one server per translator over several machines (docs/ROUTER.md)
    llmt mcp config [--print | --claude-code | --file F]   write or print the MCP client entries
    llmt mcp test [KEY...]          start each server as the Claude app does; handshake, list tools
    llmt mcp serve [KEY...] [--host H]   serve MCP over streamable HTTP on each translator's port

Backends (OpenFOAM, CalculiX, LAMMPS, Gmsh) are never installed by this tool: it reports what
is missing and points to BACKENDS.md.

Needs git and Python 3.7+ (standard library only); the venv needs Python 3.10+.
"""
